WEBVTT

00:15.680 --> 00:17.720
A daughter lost, a son found.

00:17.800 --> 00:18.840
He is yours.

00:18.920 --> 00:20.160
[Tommy] Evadne Barwell?

00:20.240 --> 00:21.920
-[gunshots firing]
-[women scream]

00:23.040 --> 00:25.000
[Nelson] Since you have proven
your commitment,

00:25.080 --> 00:29.120
Boston is now officially open
for the importation of your merchandise.

00:29.200 --> 00:32.200
Jack says a few more weeks,
and you'll be free.

00:32.280 --> 00:34.280
The stories about you come up the canal.

00:34.360 --> 00:37.880
Once you walked fine alone,
now you need a stick.

00:37.960 --> 00:39.520
[Tommy] Stay clean for two weeks.

00:40.080 --> 00:41.560
I'll write Linda another letter.

00:41.640 --> 00:43.520
[Holford] Have you recently
suffered seizures?

00:43.600 --> 00:44.960
It is tuberculoma.

00:45.040 --> 00:46.920
I am afraid it is inoperable.

00:50.600 --> 00:51.880
[pulsing music playing]

02:09.480 --> 02:13.000
Mr Shelby, I only gave
opium to your brother

02:13.080 --> 02:15.120
because he give me big trouble.

02:15.200 --> 02:16.480
He attacked my wife.

02:21.520 --> 02:22.520
[timer ticking]

02:24.720 --> 02:27.560
I'd like a pot of green tea, please.

02:27.640 --> 02:28.600
[ticking continues]

02:34.480 --> 02:35.320
[clears throat]

02:39.120 --> 02:41.480
It's taken me ten years
to build this business.

02:41.560 --> 02:44.040
Your business will be safe
if you do what I say.

02:48.040 --> 02:49.800
How much opium do you have in your cellar?

02:51.680 --> 02:52.600
Five pounds.

02:53.840 --> 02:54.920
Bring it to me.

02:56.840 --> 02:58.560
Four minutes against the clock.

03:28.880 --> 03:30.000
[exhales]

03:31.200 --> 03:32.720
[Tommy] As a Member of Parliament…

03:35.640 --> 03:37.080
for this constituency,

03:38.320 --> 03:41.960
it is my duty to take responsibility
for the welfare of my constituents.

03:42.040 --> 03:43.200
The clock is still ticking.

03:43.280 --> 03:46.760
Consumption of opium
is very prejudicial to health.

03:47.760 --> 03:49.000
Women give it to their children

03:49.080 --> 03:51.680
so they can leave them untended
while they work in the factories.

03:52.400 --> 03:54.760
Men lose their jobs
when they become addicted.

03:56.280 --> 04:02.920
[clicks tongue] From now on, you will sell
only cigarettes, cake and tea.

04:04.560 --> 04:06.760
If I hear that you're selling opium again,

04:06.840 --> 04:09.560
time will indeed run out
very quickly for you, understand?

04:09.640 --> 04:12.440
Yes. I understand. I will stop.

04:12.520 --> 04:14.480
Mr Shelby, the clock is still ticking.

04:15.240 --> 04:17.600
[in Chinese]
I don't think it's a real bomb.

04:21.440 --> 04:26.320
[in English] Please tell
your suppliers and your customers

04:27.680 --> 04:32.960
that from now on,
there will be no more opium

04:33.040 --> 04:36.120
in Small Heath or in Bordesley.

04:37.440 --> 04:38.560
Thank you for the tea.

04:50.200 --> 04:54.320
[Li in Chinese] You see.
It was not a real bomb.

05:00.400 --> 05:01.320
[water splashes]

05:11.600 --> 05:12.640
[people screaming]

05:12.720 --> 05:14.160
[dogs barking]

05:17.240 --> 05:18.840
[Tommy] You can let 'em through now.

05:18.920 --> 05:20.480
[officer] Yes, sir, Mr Shelby.

05:22.600 --> 05:25.400
You tell the pub and cafe owners
on Montague Street,

05:26.200 --> 05:29.760
if there's any further trade in powder,
there will be no more Montague Street.

05:29.840 --> 05:32.240
I'll have it demolished
and replaced by apartments.

05:32.320 --> 05:35.040
By order
of the Birmingham Urban District Council.

05:40.680 --> 05:43.880
[machine whirring]

05:49.760 --> 05:50.800
Sorry, I'm late.

05:50.880 --> 05:54.480
They closed Montague Street.
There was a gas explosion or…

05:59.600 --> 06:02.600
It would be nice if just one thing
could happen in Birmingham

06:02.680 --> 06:03.960
that wasn't our fault.

06:08.880 --> 06:11.600
I've gathered you all here today
because there is news.

06:12.520 --> 06:14.480
It is of interest to the whole family.

06:15.880 --> 06:16.880
First of all,

06:17.800 --> 06:22.920
I'd like to welcome
Finn's new wife, Mary, to the family.

06:24.080 --> 06:27.640
[smacks lips] I'm very glad
that I dragged myself out of bed for this.

06:28.360 --> 06:32.720
[sighs] There is
one more item of business.

06:32.800 --> 06:34.360
-Johnny.
-Tom.

06:35.240 --> 06:36.280
[footsteps receding]

06:36.360 --> 06:38.960
Come on. Come on, will you?

06:46.320 --> 06:47.240
Everyone,

06:49.080 --> 06:50.880
this here is Erasmus.

06:52.240 --> 06:53.440
Nobody calls me that.

06:54.080 --> 06:56.000
[clicks tongue] They call him Duke.

06:58.240 --> 07:03.920
[sighs] Twenty years ago,
at Appleby Horse Fair, I met a girl.

07:04.000 --> 07:06.040
We shared the shade of a hazel tree.

07:06.520 --> 07:07.360
[Ada exhales]

07:07.440 --> 07:10.560
Nine months later, this lad was born.

07:11.480 --> 07:12.400
[clicks tongue]

07:13.480 --> 07:14.520
This is my son.

07:15.760 --> 07:18.040
His mother died on the road.

07:18.120 --> 07:20.400
Up until now, I never tried to find him.

07:20.480 --> 07:24.520
But I'm trying
to look at life in a different way.

07:26.560 --> 07:28.080
A child is a precious thing.

07:30.920 --> 07:31.760
So I'm bringing him--

07:31.840 --> 07:34.520
Into the fucking family
with a snap of his fingers.

07:35.040 --> 07:37.080
[Tommy] No. Bringing him into the fold.

07:37.960 --> 07:40.000
He'll have to earn
membership of the family.

07:41.520 --> 07:45.080
For the moment, welcome, son.
You have a seat, go on. Sit down here.

07:52.000 --> 07:56.040
There are some mistakes I've made
that I can never redress.

07:57.280 --> 07:58.280
Some I can.

07:59.480 --> 08:01.320
Some wounds I can try to heal.

08:01.400 --> 08:03.360
New wounds you can open up.

08:05.200 --> 08:08.440
Anyway, that's the business of the day.

08:08.520 --> 08:09.680
[Tommy clears throat]

08:09.760 --> 08:11.560
Is it too early for whiskey?

08:18.760 --> 08:19.680
There you go.

08:20.960 --> 08:22.760
Shelby breakfast for you, son.

08:23.480 --> 08:24.400
I don't drink.

08:25.680 --> 08:26.760
And I'm not a Shelby.

08:27.320 --> 08:29.320
-All right? I'm a Duke.
-[Dogs scoffs]

08:29.400 --> 08:30.560
[chuckles]

08:30.640 --> 08:33.760
You're a fucking Shelby, all right.
Don't worry about that.

08:34.720 --> 08:35.560
[grunts]

08:36.360 --> 08:40.120
I think we'll need Curly and a strong rope
to break this one in, Tom.

08:40.200 --> 08:42.080
Arthur, open up the shop.

08:42.160 --> 08:44.680
Put the kid here on the blackboard,
writing up the odds.

08:45.360 --> 08:46.400
I can't write.

08:47.600 --> 08:50.440
Put the kid here on the blackboard,
wiping off the chalk.

08:50.520 --> 08:51.480
[Arthur snorts]

08:53.200 --> 08:54.040
Go on, son.

08:55.200 --> 08:56.360
Come on, then.

09:01.440 --> 09:02.400
[door opens]

09:05.280 --> 09:06.320
[door closes]

09:14.440 --> 09:15.320
Lizzie.

09:17.000 --> 09:18.240
Come on.

09:23.520 --> 09:25.760
[Duke] My father
was the Duke of Saxon Shore.

09:26.400 --> 09:28.000
My mother was a Romani queen.

09:28.080 --> 09:29.760
[Arthur] Who told you that, your mum?

09:30.920 --> 09:33.160
I don't allow people
to talk about my mother.

09:35.960 --> 09:36.880
Good for you.

09:37.600 --> 09:40.280
So let's get this right, then.
You can't read.

09:40.360 --> 09:42.560
You can't fucking write.
Nothing wrong with that.

09:42.640 --> 09:44.280
What can you do, eh?

09:45.160 --> 09:46.280
I can tell the time.

09:47.000 --> 09:48.240
Tell the time.

09:48.320 --> 09:50.080
Here, he can tell the time.

09:50.720 --> 09:51.920
Ain't that clever?

09:53.400 --> 09:55.640
It's a lot more
than what you can fucking do.

09:58.400 --> 10:00.280
[Arthur] What did you just say to me?

10:01.760 --> 10:03.240
What time is it, Mr Shelby?

10:07.760 --> 10:08.840
That's what I can do.

10:09.600 --> 10:11.200
You little bastard.

10:12.360 --> 10:13.520
[chuckles]

10:13.600 --> 10:15.080
Here. Keep it.

10:15.600 --> 10:17.600
Stop you from being late in the future.

10:24.520 --> 10:26.360
[footsteps approaching]

10:45.720 --> 10:48.800
Is there forgiveness in your heart
for Arthur Shelby?

10:50.280 --> 10:51.200
No.

10:55.040 --> 10:57.040
But there may be forgiveness from God.

10:58.200 --> 10:59.040
[clicks tongue]

10:59.960 --> 11:01.680
And you will do God's work.

11:02.440 --> 11:04.520
God is interested in you as well, Tommy.

11:05.200 --> 11:08.160
God will be with you on your journey.
Every step of the way.

11:12.600 --> 11:14.520
He may not need to take many steps.

11:28.920 --> 11:30.240
So tell me this, Linda.

11:32.240 --> 11:34.360
Is God interested in me

11:35.600 --> 11:36.720
or in my money?

11:39.000 --> 11:39.920
[exhales]

11:41.880 --> 11:43.480
I believe you run a foundation,

11:43.560 --> 11:46.720
and that your foundation
has many missions across the world.

11:47.320 --> 11:50.920
But in these times of financial crisis,
funding is hard to come by.

11:51.000 --> 11:55.120
[sniffs] So, perhaps,
your God's plan is a practical one.

11:55.200 --> 11:59.960
Perhaps he would like me
to make a donation to your foundation.

12:00.040 --> 12:03.200
And in return, he would like you

12:03.960 --> 12:06.520
to help my brother
on his road to redemption.

12:07.360 --> 12:10.120
Now, I know
that in a place of worship such as this,

12:10.200 --> 12:11.960
you would never ask how much.

12:12.040 --> 12:13.760
So I will tell you plainly.

12:14.640 --> 12:18.400
I will write your foundation
a check for £10,000…

12:18.480 --> 12:19.400
Praise the Lord.

12:20.200 --> 12:23.040
…if you agree to look kindly
on Arthur and to help him.

12:26.120 --> 12:28.360
I need to look after
everyone in the family.

12:31.040 --> 12:31.960
Do we have a deal?

12:35.640 --> 12:38.240
Your money will be spent
to do good around the world.

12:39.680 --> 12:41.720
And a mission will be named after you.

12:41.800 --> 12:42.640
[scoffs]

12:45.000 --> 12:46.720
But I'm only agreeing to help him,

12:47.680 --> 12:48.880
not sleep with him.

12:49.840 --> 12:50.760
No.

12:52.040 --> 12:55.000
No, I imagine the negotiation
for that particular favour

12:55.080 --> 12:57.240
would take a considerable amount of time.

12:58.680 --> 13:00.000
And I have an appointment.

13:02.240 --> 13:03.160
[Tommy] God bless.

13:07.560 --> 13:08.480
[indistinct chattering]

13:08.560 --> 13:11.720
[seagulls squawking]

13:26.640 --> 13:28.800
Apologies for
the initial misunderstanding.

13:31.040 --> 13:32.320
My brother dealt with it.

13:34.720 --> 13:35.560
[clicks tongue]

13:39.360 --> 13:40.640
For the care you took.

13:42.960 --> 13:44.920
Even though I succumbed to temptation?

13:45.840 --> 13:49.320
Part of the reason my brother is back
dealing with it, is down to you.

13:49.960 --> 13:50.880
You spoke to him.

13:51.560 --> 13:52.640
As a comrade.

13:52.720 --> 13:54.320
The beating is still owed to you.

13:54.400 --> 13:57.960
Do you still do that kind of work
yourself, Thomas Shelby, MP?

13:59.200 --> 14:03.080
Mr Stagg, you see,
I can use a man like you.

14:05.400 --> 14:08.360
I have friends that are in need of guns.

14:09.800 --> 14:11.520
Soon there will be a shipment

14:11.600 --> 14:15.440
of Thompson submachine guns,
coming here from Boston.

14:16.720 --> 14:19.160
I need you to unload
and store those weapons.

14:22.040 --> 14:23.640
There will also be ammunition.

14:25.080 --> 14:26.000
Like this.

14:27.720 --> 14:29.560
You have a good look.

14:29.640 --> 14:33.240
And I need you to take better care
of the guns and ammunition

14:33.760 --> 14:35.240
than you did of the powder.

14:36.840 --> 14:37.760
You understand?

14:39.240 --> 14:40.160
Previously,

14:41.560 --> 14:45.000
all of my import and export
went through Belfast docks.

14:45.600 --> 14:47.280
Now we're dealing with Boston…

14:50.080 --> 14:53.120
I am considering shifting
my supply line to Liverpool.

14:55.200 --> 14:56.520
You'd be a very rich man.

15:00.600 --> 15:02.320
Don't you ever say thank you?

15:20.840 --> 15:21.760
Thank you.

15:26.880 --> 15:28.800
Is that why you do it, Mr Shelby?

15:30.320 --> 15:32.160
Is that why you keep all this going?

15:32.680 --> 15:34.400
To help people say thank you?

15:36.120 --> 15:38.120
You could close all this down.

15:38.200 --> 15:40.040
You could leave the sport behind.

15:41.000 --> 15:43.600
You could live
like an ordinary, mortal man.

15:44.360 --> 15:45.520
On your gravestone.

15:46.640 --> 15:48.000
"An ordinary, mortal man."

15:49.920 --> 15:53.680
But instead,
you still go around collecting "please,"

15:53.760 --> 15:57.960
and "thank you," and "sorry,"
and "forgive me, Mr Shelby."

16:00.200 --> 16:01.360
That what it's all for?

16:04.520 --> 16:05.560
You want to know?

16:06.760 --> 16:08.720
You want to know why I've carried on…

16:08.800 --> 16:10.320
[inhales and exhales]

16:10.400 --> 16:11.480
…all these years?

16:13.120 --> 16:14.280
It's so I can do this.

16:19.960 --> 16:20.880
And then

16:22.360 --> 16:23.280
do this.

16:28.480 --> 16:29.400
Feel it?

16:31.400 --> 16:32.440
I feel it.

16:35.040 --> 16:36.520
Junk doesn't even come close.

16:39.080 --> 16:40.120
[sighs]

16:41.120 --> 16:42.240
Soon, Mr Stagg,

16:44.560 --> 16:46.480
when my last bit of business is done,

16:49.160 --> 16:50.160
I will, indeed,

16:51.960 --> 16:53.400
be an ordinary, mortal man.

16:56.760 --> 16:57.840
You have a good day.

17:05.280 --> 17:06.360
[Finn] Arthur.

17:06.440 --> 17:08.440
We've got a problem with the referee.

17:08.520 --> 17:11.640
He's not taking the money.
He's fucking religious or something.

17:11.720 --> 17:13.480
[Arthur] Jesus Christ.

17:15.920 --> 17:19.600
With Tommy away, you're in charge
of gambling, Arthur. What should we do?

17:20.560 --> 17:22.560
"And this they said to him,

17:23.040 --> 17:26.640
that they may have some charge
to bring against him."

17:26.720 --> 17:27.760
Arthur.

17:27.840 --> 17:30.400
This referee is threatening
to go to the police--

17:30.480 --> 17:33.680
"Jesus bent down

17:34.640 --> 17:37.320
and with one finger,
he wrote on the ground."

17:37.400 --> 17:39.240
Arthur. [sighs]

17:39.320 --> 17:40.240
Brother.

17:42.000 --> 17:43.480
People are laughing at you.

17:46.640 --> 17:49.360
So, I just phoned our holy referee again.

17:49.920 --> 17:52.240
He basically told me to fuck off.

17:52.320 --> 17:53.800
Not even basically, actually.

17:53.880 --> 17:56.840
He literally just told me… to fuck off.

17:57.360 --> 17:58.640
[Arthur] Is that right?

17:59.160 --> 18:00.080
So, do you know?

18:00.880 --> 18:02.320
[Finn sighs] For fuck's sake.

18:02.400 --> 18:05.400
-Do you know what he wrote on the ground?
-No.

18:05.480 --> 18:08.080
-Do you know? You don't know, do you?
-No. No, I don't.

18:08.160 --> 18:10.000
Billy, do you know what he wrote
on the ground?

18:10.080 --> 18:11.680
-I…
-Hmm?

18:12.560 --> 18:14.680
Do you know what Jesus wrote
on the ground?

18:14.760 --> 18:19.360
He bent down and with one finger,
he wrote on the fucking ground.

18:19.440 --> 18:21.400
You know? Do you know what he wrote?

18:21.480 --> 18:23.240
-Come on, Billy.
-[groans] No.

18:23.320 --> 18:25.080
[Finn] Arthur, what should we do?

18:26.760 --> 18:28.480
[Arthur] Go and get me the referee.

18:29.040 --> 18:31.120
Bring me the fucking referee.

18:35.240 --> 18:36.080
[Finn grunts]

18:47.400 --> 18:49.040
[both breathing heavily]

19:26.280 --> 19:27.120
[Tommy exhales]

19:30.000 --> 19:31.000
[Lizzie exhales]

19:40.680 --> 19:42.400
[Tommy] I know she's here with us.

19:45.440 --> 19:46.360
Always.

19:52.520 --> 19:54.080
But still it's just you and me.

20:02.760 --> 20:05.640
I thought it would be good
if we were in a different place.

20:08.040 --> 20:09.360
I hate that house now.

20:10.560 --> 20:12.200
I wish I could blow it up.

20:23.040 --> 20:25.440
There was a time
when we'd say nothing afterwards

20:25.520 --> 20:28.480
because we didn't have to say anything.

20:32.560 --> 20:34.680
But now we've got nothing left to say.

20:40.080 --> 20:41.160
There's business.

20:45.720 --> 20:46.840
What business?

20:50.680 --> 20:51.680
The American.

20:53.960 --> 20:55.320
He's coming to Birmingham.

20:56.360 --> 20:58.480
He's stopping over
on his way to Liverpool.

20:59.720 --> 21:01.560
He's staying with us tomorrow night.

21:02.200 --> 21:04.840
Frances knows. She's making up a menu.

21:09.320 --> 21:10.240
And then,

21:11.800 --> 21:13.160
we have to make a move.

21:17.160 --> 21:19.440
Do you want to know
what that move is, Lizzie?

21:21.800 --> 21:22.640
No.

21:25.440 --> 21:26.400
I know enough.

21:30.640 --> 21:31.960
Your book of regrets.

21:37.080 --> 21:41.040
23, 24, 52, 55.

21:43.840 --> 21:45.400
Combination to the safe.

21:49.600 --> 21:50.520
Regrets.

21:52.200 --> 21:53.120
And I'm on there.

21:54.120 --> 21:55.040
I'm on the list.

21:56.240 --> 21:59.120
On the very top of the list.

22:01.240 --> 22:02.160
[glass clinks]

22:03.840 --> 22:06.080
[Tommy clicks tongue] Yep.

22:07.520 --> 22:08.440
Yes, you are.

22:12.320 --> 22:13.840
I regret marrying you, Lizzie.

22:17.680 --> 22:19.440
Because I put you through so much.

22:20.760 --> 22:22.240
Put you through all of this.

22:23.360 --> 22:24.280
Ruby.

22:26.800 --> 22:28.160
Everything that is to come.

22:32.040 --> 22:35.200
When you married me, you married a man
and you married a curse.

22:36.440 --> 22:37.880
You have shared my fate.

22:41.840 --> 22:42.960
That is my regret.

22:47.440 --> 22:48.600
But know this, Lizzie.

22:50.720 --> 22:51.720
In this moment,

22:52.760 --> 22:53.680
in this room…

22:56.760 --> 22:57.680
I love you.

23:05.600 --> 23:07.880
You sound like
you're ticking a fucking box,

23:07.960 --> 23:10.160
and I don't know what's inside the box.

23:14.160 --> 23:17.000
Never have you let me in.

23:19.920 --> 23:22.360
Even though I know
the combination to the safe.

23:30.400 --> 23:31.960
[Lizzie breathing heavily]

24:01.720 --> 24:03.280
[Arthur] So this is him, is it?

24:03.960 --> 24:07.240
You're the one
that likes to be fucking difficult, eh?

24:07.320 --> 24:10.000
When I leave this place,
I'm going straight to the police.

24:10.080 --> 24:12.400
-[Arthur] You are?
-This man pointed a gun at me.

24:12.480 --> 24:14.480
-Who? Him there?
-[Wilfred] Yeah.

24:16.480 --> 24:18.040
Well, let's phone the police, eh?

24:19.760 --> 24:22.800
Don't worry.
We'll have this sorted out for you.

24:22.880 --> 24:24.800
Hello. Yes.

24:25.360 --> 24:26.520
Get me the police.

24:26.600 --> 24:29.080
Reports of a man
with a revolver on Watery Lane.

24:30.480 --> 24:33.680
There you go.
And you ask for Inspector Moss.

24:34.480 --> 24:38.160
Chief Superintendent Moss.

24:39.400 --> 24:42.880
He's in charge of Watery Lane
and Bordesley Green.

24:43.680 --> 24:44.560
That's right.

24:45.080 --> 24:46.080
And you see this?

24:49.000 --> 24:51.080
That's his betting credit with us.

24:52.280 --> 24:56.040
He makes a lot of money
from football matches

24:57.080 --> 25:00.760
because we give him the results
before the match.

25:00.840 --> 25:01.800
[slams dossier]

25:06.800 --> 25:07.640
[receiver bangs]

25:10.920 --> 25:14.960
On Saturday afternoon,
you take this whistle and you blow.

25:15.520 --> 25:18.320
You give a penalty
to Birmingham City in the final minute,

25:18.400 --> 25:20.640
the goalkeeper
will let the penalty go by him,

25:20.720 --> 25:23.600
and Birmingham City will win one-nil.

25:23.680 --> 25:24.960
All you gotta do is…

25:25.040 --> 25:25.880
[clears throat]

25:27.360 --> 25:28.200
[blows whistle]

25:29.080 --> 25:30.240
[snorts]

25:33.360 --> 25:34.200
No.

25:36.280 --> 25:40.040
I won't do it. If the police won't listen,
I'll go to the newspapers.

25:41.160 --> 25:42.160
I'm not afraid.

25:44.560 --> 25:46.280
I was in France.

25:46.360 --> 25:47.800
Phone Tommy, Arthur.

25:49.040 --> 25:49.880
You shut up.

25:50.960 --> 25:52.800
We're not phoning fucking Tommy.

25:53.320 --> 25:56.160
-I am dealing with this, okay?
-I'm leaving.

25:56.240 --> 25:57.960
You're not going fucking nowhere.

25:58.040 --> 25:59.920
[Wilfred] It's time one of us
stood up to you.

26:00.000 --> 26:01.920
It's not right what's been happening.

26:03.160 --> 26:05.920
I will not take money to cheat.

26:06.000 --> 26:07.440
Fucking hell.

26:07.520 --> 26:10.360
-[Arthur breathes heavily]
-In France, I ran at the wire,

26:11.040 --> 26:12.280
and I was not afraid.

26:15.000 --> 26:16.080
I am not afraid.

26:17.320 --> 26:18.480
I won't do a bad thing.

26:19.480 --> 26:21.400
I've seen too many bad things.

26:23.440 --> 26:25.320
A beating will make no difference.

26:27.120 --> 26:31.040
I know that
'cause I can see it in your fucking eyes.

26:32.040 --> 26:32.960
Oh, fuck.

26:34.240 --> 26:36.320
In the bleak midwinter…

26:36.400 --> 26:37.640
Holy Mary, Mother of God.

26:38.960 --> 26:41.160
-[exclaims]
-[Arthur] All right, Billy boy.

26:41.680 --> 26:43.840
You've been in the family long enough.

26:43.920 --> 26:46.600
Yeah. It's time for you to get bloodied.

26:46.680 --> 26:48.440
-Arthur, you can't.
-[Billy] Arthur, please.

26:48.520 --> 26:51.840
-You've been with us for long enough.
-Fuck, Arthur! Jesus Christ!

26:51.920 --> 26:54.160
Look, I can't be that man, Arthur, please.

26:54.240 --> 26:57.560
[Arthur] Either two men
die today, Billy, or one.

26:57.640 --> 26:58.640
You fucking decide.

26:58.720 --> 26:59.920
[Billy groans]

27:00.000 --> 27:02.720
-Hate him, Billy, you hate him.
-[Billy whimpers]

27:02.800 --> 27:04.560
Come on. You don't know him, Billy.

27:04.640 --> 27:06.520
He's fucking laughing at you. Come on.

27:06.600 --> 27:07.800
Hate him.

27:07.880 --> 27:09.920
-Look him in the eyes.
-[Billy] Please, no!

27:10.000 --> 27:12.320
-I can't. I can't!
-[Arthur] Look him in the eyes.

27:12.400 --> 27:13.520
Hate him!

27:13.600 --> 27:15.440
I'm sorry. Sorry.

27:15.520 --> 27:17.640
-[Billy grunts]
-[Wilfred chokes]

27:20.800 --> 27:21.880
[Billy screaming]

27:24.160 --> 27:25.240
[Wilfred gurgles]

27:29.480 --> 27:30.720
Enough. Enough. Enough.

27:33.040 --> 27:34.720
All right. Billy, come on.

27:34.800 --> 27:36.320
-[shushes]
-[Billy sobs softly]

27:38.760 --> 27:42.480
It's all right. It's all right.
It's all right. It's all right.

27:43.240 --> 27:46.760
Look at you. Look. Look at you. Look.

27:50.760 --> 27:52.120
You're bloodied now, Billy.

27:54.440 --> 27:55.640
You're bloodied now.

27:57.480 --> 27:59.360
You're not going to heaven no more.

28:00.120 --> 28:01.320
They won't let you in.

28:06.200 --> 28:10.040
Isiah, you take him to the foundry,
you ask for Mr Patches, all right?

28:10.120 --> 28:12.520
You tell him
we got some fuel for the furnace.

28:33.840 --> 28:35.360
[footsteps]

29:00.840 --> 29:01.880
[whistling tune]

29:23.120 --> 29:24.280
[whistling approaches]

29:33.840 --> 29:35.080
[footsteps approaching]

29:42.160 --> 29:43.280
Who the fuck are you?

29:46.000 --> 29:47.160
[Billy screams]

29:50.400 --> 29:52.240
-I hear…
-Please.

29:52.320 --> 29:55.080
…you're the informant
inside the Shelby organisation.

29:55.880 --> 29:56.720
No.

29:57.280 --> 29:58.680
And who the fuck I am

29:59.880 --> 30:01.480
is the man you now work for.

30:01.560 --> 30:03.480
[breath shaking] Please.

30:04.200 --> 30:06.800
I have something I need you to do
and I want to impress upon you.

30:06.880 --> 30:09.040
-To impress upon you…
-[Billy screams]

30:10.080 --> 30:12.400
-[Billy moans]
-…the seriousness of my intent.

30:13.360 --> 30:16.480
'Cause, you see, I used to do
this kind of thing for a living.

30:18.080 --> 30:20.200
And sometimes, I kind of miss it.

30:21.440 --> 30:22.520
Just like Mr Shelby.

30:22.600 --> 30:26.440
I miss the wave of electricity
you get under your scalp.

30:26.520 --> 30:29.880
I miss the taste, like metal,
on the tip of your tongue.

30:31.040 --> 30:32.840
I'm about to give you an instruction.

30:32.920 --> 30:35.960
You do as I say, you stay a man.

30:36.640 --> 30:41.600
Fail, and I will send people to serve
your balls to you on a china plate.

30:44.960 --> 30:46.040
I'll do what you say.

30:47.920 --> 30:49.400
A decision's been taken.

30:50.400 --> 30:53.040
My associates are gonna
take care of Thomas Shelby

30:53.680 --> 30:56.920
and you are gonna
give us up his brother, Arthur.

30:58.360 --> 30:59.280
Do you understand?

30:59.960 --> 31:03.120
Yes, yes. Fucking yes. Please.

31:03.200 --> 31:04.240
[panting]

31:08.160 --> 31:11.880
Only information leading to the murder
of Arthur Shelby will save you

31:11.960 --> 31:13.240
from an Italian death.

31:14.520 --> 31:17.880
'Cause it was the Italians
that taught me that above God,

31:17.960 --> 31:20.680
above children, above his wife
and above his mother…

31:22.560 --> 31:24.520
Most of all, a man loves his balls.

31:24.600 --> 31:25.680
[Billy whimpers]

31:34.800 --> 31:35.640
[groans]

31:36.760 --> 31:37.880
[breathing heavily]

31:43.080 --> 31:44.360
[sobs]

31:46.920 --> 31:48.320
[door opens]

31:52.840 --> 31:53.800
[keys clatter]

31:53.880 --> 31:54.840
[breathing heavily]

31:58.240 --> 31:59.120
[liquid spills]

32:05.480 --> 32:06.320
[sniffs]

32:14.280 --> 32:15.360
[object thuds]

32:27.400 --> 32:28.240
[sniffles]

32:36.240 --> 32:37.240
Hello, Arthur.

32:49.440 --> 32:50.600
I think we should pray.

32:53.200 --> 32:56.320
-That's how we begin this.
-You'd like to pray.

32:56.840 --> 33:00.480
The prayer I've chosen
is the Act of Contrition, version two.

33:02.600 --> 33:04.720
Are you Catholic now, Linda?

33:04.800 --> 33:05.880
You're Catholic.

33:06.560 --> 33:07.640
Quakers don't pray.

33:10.320 --> 33:12.840
Bow your head, Arthur,
and close your eyes.

33:15.200 --> 33:17.720
Recite the prayer. You know it well
from when you were a boy.

33:17.800 --> 33:19.880
My mind's all dried up with junk, though.

33:20.600 --> 33:21.720
And shot full of fuck…

33:22.440 --> 33:23.920
Shot full of holes. It's…

33:27.360 --> 33:29.160
Linda, please.

33:30.080 --> 33:32.760
[Linda] It's in there somewhere, Arthur.
It's like a song.

33:32.840 --> 33:33.760
[Arthur] Yeah.

33:35.640 --> 33:37.480
-Somewhere.
-Together, we'll find it.

33:38.040 --> 33:40.520
Digging for the words
will help clean your soul.

33:42.720 --> 33:43.640
I'll begin it.

33:46.280 --> 33:49.400
"Forgive me my sins, oh, Lord,
forgive me my sins."

33:50.000 --> 33:51.160
"The sins of my youth…"

33:52.240 --> 33:54.600
"The sins of my youth, the sins of my age,

33:55.360 --> 33:56.560
the sins of my soul."

33:58.760 --> 34:00.000
"The sins of my body…"

34:01.440 --> 34:04.120
"The sins I know, the sins I know not."

34:05.560 --> 34:07.760
"The sins I have concealed for so long."

34:08.440 --> 34:09.480
"For so…" Fuck…

34:10.320 --> 34:11.240
"For so long."

34:31.800 --> 34:33.200
Caught him stealing a car.

34:34.000 --> 34:36.520
And he's got a stack of cash
from the betting shop.

34:49.720 --> 34:51.160
Steal from who you want.

34:52.040 --> 34:53.080
Don't steal from me.

34:55.880 --> 34:56.800
Here you are.

34:59.080 --> 35:02.360
Get a train to wherever the fuck
you want to go and get out.

35:02.440 --> 35:04.560
-I don't ride trains.
-[Tommy] That a fact?

35:07.880 --> 35:09.720
Well, Curly has a two-wheeled wagon.

35:10.760 --> 35:12.200
What am I, a tinker?

35:12.280 --> 35:13.320
I need four wheels.

35:13.920 --> 35:15.960
All right? And a horse for the hills.

35:20.000 --> 35:20.920
Which hills?

35:21.840 --> 35:22.840
All of them.

35:23.480 --> 35:24.800
All the hills of England.

35:26.120 --> 35:26.960
[scoffs]

35:29.760 --> 35:31.040
Why do you want to leave?

35:35.160 --> 35:37.480
I didn't take to that work
in the betting shop.

35:41.360 --> 35:42.920
Well, you heard him, Charlie.

35:43.600 --> 35:46.480
Get my dad's old four-wheeled wagon
and two strong ponies.

35:47.080 --> 35:48.000
All right.

35:48.600 --> 35:50.680
[Charlie] Curly. Get here.

35:56.960 --> 36:00.080
Before you go, you want to know
the truth about yourself?

36:02.480 --> 36:03.320
No.

36:03.880 --> 36:04.800
Who does?

36:06.800 --> 36:08.480
Right, well, I'm gonna tell you.

36:09.280 --> 36:13.040
That spring in Appleby Fair,
your mother stole my watch and chain.

36:13.120 --> 36:14.880
You're from a long line of thieves.

36:15.880 --> 36:19.480
The watch had the words
"Saxon Shore" carved in it.

36:19.560 --> 36:22.360
Stole it myself
from a drunk when I was a kid.

36:23.840 --> 36:27.600
I imagine she told you, your dad
was the Duke of the Saxon Shore. Well…

36:29.440 --> 36:30.680
[clicks tongue] I am the Duke.

36:30.760 --> 36:31.840
It was my watch.

36:32.920 --> 36:34.000
I'm your father.

36:36.600 --> 36:37.640
That's the truth.

36:39.040 --> 36:42.600
When her dad found out, he shot me
in the chest with a squirrel gun.

36:43.680 --> 36:48.560
A scar, a stolen watch
and a story she made up.

36:50.480 --> 36:53.960
That's all you need to know about yourself
before you get on the road.

37:06.520 --> 37:08.760
Esme tells me the spirits favour you.

37:10.640 --> 37:12.320
That the spirit is in you.

37:12.400 --> 37:15.280
She tried to sell me like
one of those horses, didn't she?

37:16.000 --> 37:17.440
How much did you pay for me?

37:19.440 --> 37:21.040
I have no use for gold any more.

37:22.000 --> 37:23.280
But if you are a horse,

37:24.120 --> 37:25.480
you're in the right place.

37:27.000 --> 37:27.920
Curly!

37:30.360 --> 37:31.640
Curly, hurry up!

37:32.720 --> 37:34.240
This boy has hills to climb.

37:37.800 --> 37:39.080
I remember that watch.

37:41.680 --> 37:42.920
Oh, yeah?

37:44.360 --> 37:46.120
She used to wear it over her heart.

37:49.520 --> 37:50.640
We buried it with her.

37:54.480 --> 37:55.400
Tom.

37:55.480 --> 37:57.800
The old wagon's
right front wheel is fucked, Tom.

37:57.880 --> 37:59.200
Standing in the wet.

38:00.880 --> 38:02.240
Put a new wheel on, Curly.

38:09.120 --> 38:10.200
They fix wagons here.

38:12.160 --> 38:14.120
Good families come from the New Forest,

38:15.040 --> 38:16.520
get their wagons fixed,

38:16.600 --> 38:18.520
and fresh horses before the fairs.

38:22.240 --> 38:23.120
Yeah.

38:23.640 --> 38:24.840
Yeah, I like it here.

38:25.880 --> 38:27.800
Like it better than that betting shop.

38:30.800 --> 38:31.720
[Tommy] Why?

38:32.680 --> 38:33.600
People.

38:34.760 --> 38:35.840
People piss me off.

38:38.240 --> 38:40.560
There are a lot of people
in that betting shop.

38:41.640 --> 38:43.960
So far, here, what? I've only counted two.

38:44.040 --> 38:44.880
[Tommy] Mmm-hmm.

38:46.280 --> 38:49.320
Charlie and Curly.
The rest is dogs and horses.

38:49.400 --> 38:50.880
Curly's half horse himself.

38:52.480 --> 38:53.400
[Duke] Dogs are okay.

38:54.640 --> 38:56.640
Horses are better than people, mind you.

39:00.240 --> 39:02.480
There's work here
for a man who knows horses.

39:06.000 --> 39:06.920
Unknown.

39:08.400 --> 39:10.240
I want to remain completely unknown.

39:11.160 --> 39:14.680
You'd be in the right place for that
as well. No one knows anyone here.

39:16.320 --> 39:18.240
Hey, mister, save that wheel a minute.

39:20.520 --> 39:21.600
Where would I stay?

39:23.360 --> 39:24.280
The stables.

39:25.120 --> 39:26.600
With the other stallions.

39:27.840 --> 39:31.160
Now that Finn is married off,
plenty of girls around here.

39:32.040 --> 39:34.800
Fathers are mostly unarmed.

39:38.920 --> 39:40.960
I have a future for you, Duke.

39:43.400 --> 39:44.680
You already have a son.

39:46.840 --> 39:48.200
My business has two sides.

39:49.600 --> 39:50.800
Light and dark.

39:51.960 --> 39:53.320
I'll need someone for each.

39:54.840 --> 39:56.600
And I'm dark, am I?

39:58.280 --> 40:00.960
I've realised we don't get
to choose which one we are.

40:02.760 --> 40:03.840
Dark knows dark.

40:05.560 --> 40:07.520
And my affairs, both light and dark,

40:09.280 --> 40:10.560
will need settling soon.

40:12.920 --> 40:13.920
Curly?

40:14.760 --> 40:17.840
Find a shovel
for the Duke of the Saxon Shore here.

40:18.640 --> 40:21.000
-Get him shovelling shit.
-[chuckles]

40:21.080 --> 40:23.000
[Tommy] And put some petrol in the boat.

40:23.080 --> 40:25.040
I have to meet a lady in Solihull.

40:25.520 --> 40:26.760
["One Silver Dollar" playing]

40:26.840 --> 40:29.640
♪ One silver dollar ♪

40:30.120 --> 40:33.360
♪ Bright silver dollar ♪

40:33.880 --> 40:39.560
♪ Changing hands, changing hands ♪

40:40.520 --> 40:44.200
♪ Spent for a beer he's drinking ♪

40:44.280 --> 40:47.720
♪ Won by a gambler's lust ♪

40:47.960 --> 40:52.000
♪ Pierced by an outlaw's bullet ♪

40:52.080 --> 40:57.800
♪ And lost in the blood red dust ♪

40:59.160 --> 41:02.200
♪ One silver dollar ♪

41:02.280 --> 41:04.840
♪ One silver dollar ♪

41:04.920 --> 41:05.920
Take a look at her.

41:08.120 --> 41:10.320
Now imagine ten people living on-site.

41:12.680 --> 41:14.160
Step on, have a look inside.

41:20.240 --> 41:22.520
I've had a response
from the Guinness Trust

41:23.320 --> 41:25.520
about building charitable housing

41:26.120 --> 41:28.960
on two sites along the canal network

41:29.440 --> 41:32.840
between London, Birmingham and Liverpool.

41:33.680 --> 41:36.760
This lock here will be one of the sites.

41:37.840 --> 41:41.040
I have the permission.
Just need the finance.

41:43.440 --> 41:46.720
I know that you and your husband,
Bryan Guinness, are estranged.

41:46.800 --> 41:50.440
But I understand you still have
influence in the Guinness family.

41:50.520 --> 41:51.560
[scoffs]

41:51.640 --> 41:54.320
Your support might help them
make their decision.

41:54.400 --> 41:55.320
Will you help me?

42:05.640 --> 42:07.720
I've booked a suite in a hotel
a mile from here.

42:09.320 --> 42:11.000
My chauffeur will take us there.

42:13.080 --> 42:16.200
You look quite the thing
dressed like that, like a working man.

42:16.720 --> 42:19.840
They'll probably show you
to the coal house to make your delivery.

42:20.840 --> 42:22.480
Yep, they probably will.

42:26.080 --> 42:27.800
Oswald has fucked your wife, so,

42:27.880 --> 42:30.680
my suggestion is about
balance and proportion.

42:31.760 --> 42:33.040
It would be only fair.

42:37.200 --> 42:38.280
Can I assume

42:39.520 --> 42:40.760
I have your support?

42:44.840 --> 42:48.360
This isn't about charitable housing,
this is about changing the world.

42:49.240 --> 42:51.120
It's about a different kind of trust.

42:51.960 --> 42:53.160
Absolute trust.

42:54.760 --> 42:56.600
We have important work ahead of us.

42:59.280 --> 43:02.240
It's much harder to lie with your body
than with your words.

43:03.440 --> 43:04.640
This I have learned.

43:12.720 --> 43:14.560
Mostly, I do whatever I want to do.

43:15.840 --> 43:17.800
Sometimes I do things for the cause.

43:18.520 --> 43:19.880
In this case, it's both.

43:23.560 --> 43:24.400
Come.

43:27.000 --> 43:28.480
[both breathing heavily]

43:32.440 --> 43:33.440
Oh, my God!

43:51.320 --> 43:53.000
In the interests of absolute clarity,

43:53.080 --> 43:57.080
that is simply the English aristocracy's
way of shaking hands.

43:58.240 --> 43:59.200
[exhales]

44:01.040 --> 44:01.960
So…

44:03.080 --> 44:04.080
Welcome.

44:23.520 --> 44:24.720
[exhales]

44:35.000 --> 44:36.440
["Unmade" playing]

44:47.320 --> 44:48.160
[exhales]

44:49.800 --> 44:51.640
[vocalising]

44:57.120 --> 45:03.360
♪ Come under my wings, little bird ♪

45:04.640 --> 45:10.760
♪ Come under my wings, little bird ♪

45:12.920 --> 45:13.760
[grunts]

45:17.680 --> 45:18.800
[gasping]

45:20.920 --> 45:26.880
♪ Unmade ♪

45:28.240 --> 45:32.160
♪ Unmade ♪

45:34.760 --> 45:41.240
♪ I swear that there's nothing ♪

45:42.120 --> 45:47.040
♪ Up my sleeves ♪

45:50.160 --> 45:54.040
♪ And then back again ♪

45:56.960 --> 46:02.720
♪ I swear there's nothing ♪

46:05.800 --> 46:09.040
♪ Unmade ♪

46:11.360 --> 46:12.240
[lighter clicks]

46:26.680 --> 46:31.800
♪ There's no faces ♪

46:34.880 --> 46:39.120
♪ Won't grow back again ♪

46:41.040 --> 46:42.000
[gasps]

46:42.200 --> 46:46.640
♪ Broken pieces ♪

46:49.200 --> 46:50.480
[Polly] If you do this thing,

46:52.520 --> 46:54.240
the possibility of war

46:54.840 --> 46:56.240
you have to consider.

47:02.240 --> 47:04.040
[Michael] It was the ambitions
and strategies

47:04.120 --> 47:05.360
of one man that caused this.

47:09.160 --> 47:11.640
[Polly] There will be a war in this family

47:12.320 --> 47:13.960
and one of you will die.

47:14.520 --> 47:17.720
♪ Nothing ♪

47:19.640 --> 47:20.680
[breathing heavily]

47:20.760 --> 47:24.440
♪ Won't grow back again ♪

47:27.160 --> 47:32.280
♪ I swear there's nothing ♪

47:40.120 --> 47:42.760
We need to leave early
to catch the first train to Liverpool.

47:42.840 --> 47:44.240
-Yes?
-[Tommy] Yep.

47:45.360 --> 47:47.040
So we eat early, finish early.

47:52.480 --> 47:54.520
You changed the combination of the safe.

47:55.920 --> 47:56.840
Why?

47:57.880 --> 47:59.240
Have you got new secrets?

48:00.360 --> 48:07.000
With this new business at hand,
there are some things that I cannot share.

48:07.600 --> 48:08.600
What things?

48:11.960 --> 48:12.800
[glass thuds]

48:14.960 --> 48:16.120
What are those tablets?

48:16.760 --> 48:17.920
Doctor gave 'em to me.

48:18.480 --> 48:19.520
Painkillers?

48:19.600 --> 48:21.640
-Yep.
-What pain?

48:23.240 --> 48:25.040
Any pain that comes, Lizzie. [sighs]

48:48.520 --> 48:51.880
When you're ready, I want you to tell me
everything that's going on.

48:55.280 --> 48:59.120
It's like the clock stopped ticking
and I'm waiting for the bomb to explode.

49:03.640 --> 49:05.360
We're in that quiet minute.

49:12.120 --> 49:13.000
Tommy?

49:21.560 --> 49:22.920
That's where we live now.

49:25.440 --> 49:26.720
When I know everything,

49:28.840 --> 49:30.400
I will tell you everything.

49:47.240 --> 49:49.240
[Nelson] No, Gina's running wild, you see.

49:49.320 --> 49:51.880
Harrods, dope, amphetamines,
lords and ladies,

49:51.960 --> 49:54.040
the whole English aristocracy thing.

49:54.120 --> 49:55.640
Fuck wine. Whiskey.

49:56.520 --> 49:59.000
-Shelby, you having whiskey?
-I'll stay on wine.

49:59.080 --> 50:01.560
[Nelson] Fuck wine.
More whiskey. I'm celebrating.

50:02.160 --> 50:05.560
Celebration, you know?
Getting off this fucking island.

50:05.640 --> 50:09.720
You see, the thing with England…
The currency here, it's not money.

50:09.800 --> 50:12.080
Nah. You got bored of money
a long time ago.

50:13.640 --> 50:15.960
'Cause, anyone can have money.
You can fucking…

50:19.360 --> 50:21.280
You can fucking find money in the mud.

50:22.240 --> 50:23.360
You can forge money.

50:24.480 --> 50:26.960
Mr Shelby, you can steal money,
am I right?

50:28.240 --> 50:29.280
The currency here,

50:30.560 --> 50:31.400
it's blood.

50:33.920 --> 50:36.400
And Mr Shelby knows that
better than all of them.

50:36.920 --> 50:39.480
Blood here is like wine,
like vintage wine in that bottle.

50:39.560 --> 50:41.080
It's the label.

50:41.160 --> 50:44.440
It's the terroir.
It's the grape that makes the wine.

50:44.520 --> 50:46.760
Who fucking cares
about the glass around it?

50:46.840 --> 50:48.800
And you, my friend, you're an American.

50:49.280 --> 50:51.640
You fucking smash the glass,

50:51.720 --> 50:55.440
you spill the blood and you spend
their currency to get what you want.

50:57.160 --> 50:58.080
Am I right?

51:00.440 --> 51:02.040
When you come to America,

51:02.680 --> 51:04.400
I will show you things.

51:05.000 --> 51:06.280
You're going to America?

51:08.840 --> 51:12.040
To Canada, Lizzie,
to collect payment for the shipment.

51:12.600 --> 51:14.080
I need to do it myself.

51:15.440 --> 51:16.840
And who will be going with you?

51:16.920 --> 51:19.400
Michael will be there to watch his back.

51:19.480 --> 51:22.040
Another journey, Tommy?

51:22.680 --> 51:26.440
Five million dollars, Mrs Shelby.
Worth a little cruise, don't you think?

51:30.480 --> 51:32.000
You know, whiskey does talk,

51:33.240 --> 51:35.200
Mr Nelson, and sometimes whiskey is

51:36.400 --> 51:37.320
very eloquent.

51:39.520 --> 51:43.640
But five million dollars, Mr Nelson…

51:45.480 --> 51:46.640
Now that is a legacy.

51:49.040 --> 51:50.200
And when I come back,

51:51.280 --> 51:52.440
I will know everything.

51:54.840 --> 51:59.840
I see myself
so clearly in you, Thomas Shelby.

52:01.520 --> 52:04.680
You are a man
with a bright and glittering future.

52:04.760 --> 52:07.040
-[door opens]
-[footsteps approaching]

52:08.160 --> 52:10.560
[Frances] Mr Shelby,
there's a car coming up the drive.

52:10.640 --> 52:11.720
A Rolls Royce.

52:12.400 --> 52:14.200
Were you expecting more guests?

52:15.840 --> 52:16.720
No.

52:24.640 --> 52:25.800
Excuse me.

52:33.600 --> 52:36.120
We were on our way
to my constituency in Smethwick

52:36.200 --> 52:39.680
and I heard our American friend
was in Birmingham and he was coming here.

52:40.320 --> 52:43.720
So we came to say one last farewell.

52:47.040 --> 52:49.600
Champagne. We have much to celebrate.

52:58.080 --> 53:01.160
It's not that I thought Mr Shelby
wouldn't give you an excellent send-off,

53:01.240 --> 53:02.240
I just felt,

53:02.880 --> 53:08.480
since telegrams and wires and letters
can so easily be intercepted,

53:09.000 --> 53:13.120
we might confirm all that we've achieved
during your visit over champagne.

53:14.440 --> 53:17.520
It is remarkable how quickly
our relationships have developed.

53:18.120 --> 53:19.920
So many triangles in this room.

53:21.120 --> 53:24.000
Everyone, except for Mr Nelson,
is the point of a triangle.

53:25.800 --> 53:27.200
How am I part of a triangle?

53:27.760 --> 53:31.560
Mr Nelson, you have all that you came for?

53:31.640 --> 53:33.800
I have confirmation
that the future of Europe

53:33.880 --> 53:36.600
is in the hands of men like yourselves.

53:37.440 --> 53:41.360
And that urgent conversations
between Washington, Rome

53:41.440 --> 53:43.760
and, of course, Berlin can now begin.

53:45.400 --> 53:48.320
A two-week visit
may have changed the course of history.

53:49.720 --> 53:51.240
We all got what we wanted.

53:51.320 --> 53:52.240
Yes.

53:53.160 --> 53:56.360
And I got what I have wanted
from the moment I set eyes on it.

54:02.240 --> 54:04.880
Elizabeth, you are a very lucky woman.

54:06.280 --> 54:09.040
To have each day
what I have only sampled once.

54:12.000 --> 54:12.880
[scoffs]

54:30.600 --> 54:31.600
[exhales]

54:33.120 --> 54:36.360
Forgive us, Mr Nelson.
That was a necessary bit of housekeeping.

54:42.400 --> 54:43.320
Thomas,

54:45.000 --> 54:47.080
we do so hate to be indiscreet,

54:48.320 --> 54:52.560
but we have told you many times,
if you were to seek power in these days

54:53.400 --> 54:57.240
of shiny magazines
and society photographs,

54:57.920 --> 55:01.280
sooner or later, you will have to find
a spouse who's more suitable.

55:02.280 --> 55:04.040
A woman with Lizzie's past

55:04.120 --> 55:06.760
and personal history
really isn't suitable.

55:09.440 --> 55:11.320
She doesn't deserve you, Mr Shelby.

55:35.520 --> 55:39.720
You know, the thing is, Mosley,
you're right.

55:43.080 --> 55:44.960
You're right, she doesn't deserve me.

55:49.960 --> 55:51.520
She doesn't deserve what I am.

55:54.160 --> 55:56.360
She doesn't deserve what I will become.

55:56.920 --> 55:58.120
What will you become?

55:59.120 --> 56:01.240
Truth is, I belong here at this table

56:02.000 --> 56:03.560
with fuckers like you.

56:06.600 --> 56:07.520
She doesn't.

56:11.160 --> 56:12.720
For all I try to hide it…

56:14.680 --> 56:16.360
[scoffs] I'm just one of you.

56:21.240 --> 56:23.400
Could there be a sadder ending, eh?

56:24.080 --> 56:28.160
♪ Take a little walk
To the edge of town ♪

56:28.240 --> 56:29.080
[clicks tongue]

56:29.160 --> 56:32.400
♪ And go across the tracks ♪

56:35.200 --> 56:38.200
♪ Where the viaduct looms ♪

56:38.280 --> 56:41.200
♪ Like a bird of doom ♪

56:41.320 --> 56:45.000
♪ As it shifts and cracks ♪

56:47.320 --> 56:53.200
♪ Where secrets lie
In the border fires ♪

56:53.280 --> 56:56.840
♪ In the humming wires ♪

56:57.360 --> 57:01.080
♪ Hey man, you know ♪

57:01.160 --> 57:04.920
♪ You're never coming back ♪

57:05.000 --> 57:08.160
♪ Past the square
Past the bridge ♪

57:08.240 --> 57:12.240
♪ Past the mills
And the stacks ♪

57:12.320 --> 57:14.840
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

57:14.920 --> 57:17.360
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

57:17.440 --> 57:20.640
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

57:20.720 --> 57:24.360
♪ A red right hand ♪

57:24.440 --> 57:26.360
[priest] I'm here
on behalf of your wife, Gina,

57:26.440 --> 57:27.360
and Jack Nelson.

57:28.240 --> 57:30.440
Mr Nelson's prepared
to get you out of here.

57:31.200 --> 57:33.240
But first he needs
an answer to a question.

57:35.400 --> 57:36.800
If the answer is yes,

57:38.560 --> 57:39.560
you'd be released.

57:42.080 --> 57:43.160
If the answer is no,

57:44.760 --> 57:45.680
you'll stay.

57:49.120 --> 57:50.560
I have consulted my mother.

57:51.960 --> 57:52.960
Your mother's dead.

57:55.640 --> 57:57.400
Nevertheless, I've consulted her.

58:01.080 --> 58:02.000
And, yes,

58:03.760 --> 58:06.840
when I'm released,
it is my intention to kill Tommy Shelby.

58:11.160 --> 58:14.360
♪ He's a god, he's a man ♪

58:14.440 --> 58:17.960
♪ He's a ghost, he's a guru ♪

58:18.040 --> 58:20.760
♪ And they're whispering his name ♪

58:21.680 --> 58:24.680
♪ Through the disappearing land ♪

58:25.440 --> 58:28.120
♪ But hidden in his coat ♪

58:29.920 --> 58:33.320
♪ Is a red right hand ♪

58:42.560 --> 58:44.760
♪ You don't have no money? ♪

58:45.600 --> 58:48.760
♪ Well, he'll get you some ♪

58:50.120 --> 58:52.960
♪ You don't have no car? ♪

58:53.520 --> 58:55.000
♪ He'll get you one ♪
